            "paragraph": "In undisturbed areas of Southeast Alaska, continuous forest cover extends from the shoreline up to the treeline. This inhibits low-elevation avalanches, defined by those originating below the treeline, and hazards are largely confined to large high-elevation avalanches that are able to clear forest corridors and extend their runout down to the ocean.",
